WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.270
Speaker 1: Welcome back to The David Pakman
Show, I am Ferren cousins from Ring of Fire,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.090
sitting in for David Pakman today.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:15.730
The Dixie fire ravaging out there in the state
of California this week essentially swallowed

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.990
up an entire town, the town of Greenville.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.200
It was an old mining town has been around
for ages.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:28.290
Small population estimated to be about twelve
hundred, and that fire absolutely incinerated

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:33.200
and destroyed the downtown of this area.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.840
The Dixie fire and of course, many homes and
all of that, the town is destroyed, much like

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.620
Paradise was several years ago with that wildfire.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:49.710
And now we have another town that is on the
verge of not even existing because of this

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:50.710
fire.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.880
Dixie Fire's been raging for three weeks now.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:01:00.780
And it is just one of one of one of my numbers
here, one of 97 wildfires.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:07.190
Currently in the United States, across 13
different states, we have 97 wildfires right

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.680
now ravaging the United States.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:17.330
Twenty thousand active firefighters out there
trying to put out the flames or.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.049
This is climate change.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:26.380
Let's be honest, the heat dome that we saw
over the Pacific Northwest earlier this summer,

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.890
that's climate change.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:35.119
We have such extreme temperatures over on
the west coast, the northern west coast.

00:01:35.119 --> 00:01:40.440
That we've literally had billions of sea creatures.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:45.950
That have died because of the extreme change
in the water temperature.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:51.409
And to make matters worse, with the Dixie
fire and other fires, we're having another

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:57.939
weather event, you know, strong gusting winds,
you know, 30, 40 miles an hour, that is making

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:00.590
it difficult for firefighters to be able to
get there.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:06.010
And, of course, it's making it easier for
the fire to spread.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:10.869
And based on the reporting that I've seen,
it does appear.

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:17.409
That this fire, much like the one that destroyed
the town of Paradise, was possibly started

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:24.980
by faulty equipment from California energy
company P, G and E..

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.260
This one they're saying there, they believe
there was a branch laying on a piece of equipment

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.829
that could have sparked and then caused the
fire.

00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:41.959
Obviously, it's a little too soon to make
bold accusations as to you know, PG&amp;E was

00:02:41.959 --> 00:02:43.769
definitely at fault for this.

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:46.590
First, we got to work on getting the flames
out.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.579
We've got to conduct the investigations.

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:52.269
We've got to figure out what exactly is happening
here.

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:54.629
So that's what's being reported.

00:02:54.629 --> 00:02:58.689
Again, can't necessarily make one claim one
way or another.

00:02:58.689 --> 00:03:05.870
But what we do have to acknowledge, the claim
we can make is that extreme events like this,

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.059
all of these fires, not just the Dixie fire.

00:03:09.059 --> 00:03:12.559
This is what climate change looks like.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:19.459
We have watched all through twenty twenty
one, to be honest with you, as climate change.

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:22.640
Isn't knocking at our door.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:28.629
It's bursting through that door and saying,
I am here.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:35.790
Winter Storm Yurie in Texas, that was climate
change, saying, Here I am, look at me.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:42.650
The heat dome, here I am, the fires that,
of course, result from the droughts and the

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:45.639
extreme heat.

00:03:45.639 --> 00:03:50.829
I am here is what climate change is telling
us.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:59.729
Now, we have an administration now that understands
this, we just went four years with an administration

00:03:59.729 --> 00:04:05.200
that at one point had said that climate change
was a hoax by the Chinese.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:12.559
And the Trump administration actively worked
to roll back environmental protections, emission

00:04:12.559 --> 00:04:20.780
reductions, fuel efficiency, all for no other
reason than he wanted to undo parts of President

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.540
Obama's environmental legacy.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.190
And Republicans cheered this stuff on, they
were happy about it.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:32.170
Oh, boy, he's repealing the mat standard.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:37.310
So there's going to be more mercury in our
air.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:41.850
They were happy about these things.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.250
But climate change is here.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:50.440
I know, I know, I know, I know the study from
twenty eighteen saying we got 12 years till

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.400
the worst effects as climate change might
not just hit us, but might also become the

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.400
norm.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.150
Well, guess what?

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:01.470
That was three years ago that that came out.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:06.810
And we essentially had three years at that
point and two years prior to that of backpedaling

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.790
on the issue of climate change.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:14.280
More emissions, even though we had the pandemic
last year, global emissions actually still

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.970
increased.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:20.250
We're not getting better yet.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.430
But we can.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:27.950
There is still time and with an administration
that understands the dangers of this, have

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.250
they gone as far as I want them to on the
issue of climate change?

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.690
Absolutely not.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:38.390
Like, really not even close to what needs
to happen.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:44.310
But at least we're finally moving in the right
direction and you can't be upset about that,

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.780
we can be frustrated that we're not doing
everything that needs to be done yet.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.850
And that's why we keep pushing and that's
why we keep fighting.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:52.020
Here's a little bit of silver lining, though,

